  data:  # e63f
    kind: work_item  # e63f
    title: "nightly test-matrix leg marked failed on runner Docker-archive timeout despite all tests passing (context deadline exceeded)"  # e63f
    status: todo_soft  # e63f
    priority: 3  # e63f
    parent:  # e63f
    tags:  # e63f
    - ci_infrastructure  # e63f
    isbefore: []  # e63f
    duplicate_of: []  # e63f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e63f
    pr_ref:  # e63f
    description: "OBSERVED 2026-06-17 (human-reported): the nightly.yml test-matrix (Python 3.13) leg ran all 19,083 collected items to completion — output reached [ 99%] with only skips (s) and xfailed (x), ZERO failures (F) — then the JOB was marked FAILED with a runner-side error at teardown:\n\n  ⚙️ [runner]: context deadline exceeded\n  Get \"http://%2Fvar%2Frun%2Fdocker.sock/v1.51/containers/<id>/archive?path=%2Fvar%2Frun%2Fact%2Fworkflow%2FSUMMARY.md\": context deadline exceeded\n  Get \"...archive?path=...pathcmd.txt\": context deadline exceeded\n\nSo the tests PASSED; the Forgejo-Actions/act runner timed out talking to the Docker socket while archiving the workflow artifacts (SUMMARY.md, pathcmd.txt) at job teardown, and that transient infra timeout marked the leg failed. CONSEQUENCE: a green multi-Python matrix run produces a false andon-cord / red nightly, prompting wasted investigation (and could mask a real failure under the same symptom). NOT a code defect — confirmed the change on dev (WI-moriz, f32afafd9a) is 3.13-clean (its tests passed in this very leg).\n\nTHEME: same CI runner contention/timeout family as INV-rahib (auto-pr declaring a false explicit-failure under concurrent CI activity / nightly-overlap). RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT: INV-rahib is the auto-pr convergence layer; this is a nightly job-teardown artifact-archival timeout. Cross-link, not fold.\n\nCANDIDATE MITIGATIONS: (a) retry the artifact-archival / increase the runner Docker context deadline; (b) make the matrix leg's pass/fail key off the pytest exit code rather than the teardown archival step; (c) job-level retry for transient runner errors (distinguish 'tests failed' from 'runner errored'); (d) reduce per-leg artifact size if SUMMARY.md/pathcmd.txt archival is the bottleneck. Touches .github/workflows/nightly.yml (CI workflow; sensitive — coordinate)."  # e63f
    fields: {}  # e63f
- op: discuss  # 725b
  at: '2026-06-17T16:00:57Z'  # 725b
  by: agent  # 725b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 725b
  clock: 2  # 725b
  nonce: 725b  # 725b
  message: "INVESTIGATION (2026-06-17, recon + my verification of nightly.yml): the recon's proposed fix (gate the job verdict on pytest's exit code via 'pytest || TEST_EXIT_CODE=$?; exit $TEST_EXIT_CODE') is a NO-OP for this failure. The pytest step (nightly.yml:73-100) SUCCEEDED (exit 0, 19083 passed); the job died in the runner's POST-JOB teardown archiving /var/run/act/workflow/SUMMARY.md + pathcmd.txt off the Docker socket ('context deadline exceeded'). That teardown runs AFTER the step, so the step's exit code is irrelevant; SUMMARY.md/pathcmd.txt are act-runner internals not controllable from YAML. ALSO: nightly already has a test-matrix-retry job (112-194, runs on test-matrix failure/cancelled) AND the report job (258-263) sets nightly/test-matrix=success if PRIMARY **OR** RETRY succeeded — a correctly-designed transient-recovery mechanism that already exists. So this is a TRANSIENT RUNNER-INFRA flake (Docker-socket deadline under load), not a workflow-logic bug. NO clean, confident, locally-verifiable in-repo fix. OPEN QUESTION (need the run data): did test-matrix-retry run and succeed (=> commit status nightly/test-matrix was GREEN, and the red is only the cosmetic primary-job tile in the Actions UI), or did the retry ALSO teardown-flake (=> commit status RED)? Only in-repo lever I can see: reduce matrix max-parallel to lessen Docker-socket contention (tradeoff: slower nightly; speculative, may not fix). The real fix is runner config (raise the act Docker archival deadline), which is out-of-repo. Recommend: confirm retry-recovery from the actual nightly run before any change."  # 725b
