  message: "RESOLVED — working as designed; no change. Human confirmed (2026-06-17) that test-matrix-retry DID run and succeed for the flaked 3.13 leg. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: the report job (nightly.yml:258-263) sets the nightly/test-matrix COMMIT STATUS to success when PRIMARY **OR** RETRY succeeded; since the retry succeeded, the authoritative commit status was GREEN. The only artifact was the cosmetic red primary-job tile in the Actions UI (the transient runner-teardown 'context deadline exceeded' on the primary 3.13 leg) — which is the expected appearance when a transient flake is recovered by the existing retry path, not a downstream failure. The recon's proposed step-exit-code fix was additionally a no-op (the failure is in post-job teardown, after the pytest step which exited 0). No workflow change warranted: the test-matrix-retry + OR-verdict recovery mechanism already converges transient single-leg runner flakes to a green verdict. If the teardown-flake FREQUENCY ever becomes a nuisance, the only in-repo lever is reducing matrix max-parallel to cut Docker-socket contention (tradeoff: slower nightly); the proper fix is runner config (raise the act Docker archival deadline), which is out-of-repo. Cross-ref INV-rahib (same runner-contention family)."  # 31b4
